{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1231072-help-with-creating-a-good-changeling-adventure","id":1231072,"title":"Help with creating a good Changeling adventure","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-29T05:16:17-07:00","id":1231072,"title":"Help with creating a good Changeling adventure","content":"So it's time to start writing a sandbox for Changeling. Which I'm very much looking forward to, since it's one of those rpg's I have always wanted to play, but never really been able.<br /> <br /> So before I start writing, I thought that I could ask the community about tips. Like best way to introduce game mechanics in game, or just cool story ideas. Best enemies to use, or any other cool ideas.<br /> <br /> For information purposes my players usually play.<br /> <br /> *Combat heavy, intimidation criminal or dirty cop<br /> *Combat backstabbing face<br /> *Grotesque, like nosferatu<br /> * Academic, doctor or support.<br /> <br /> My plan was to make them create a mortal character and have them start in the hedge, with little memory of what has happened to them. Just the strong urge to run, and a longing for home. And from there introduce game mechanics and the world slowly and in game.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12759-sleepy","name":"Sleepy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T13:29:32-07:00","id":1231204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sleepy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1231072-help-with-creating-a-good-changeling-adventure#post1231072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it's time to start writing a sandbox for Changeling. Which I'm very much looking forward to, since it's one of those rpg's I have always wanted to play, but never really been able.<br /> <br /> So before I start writing, I thought that I could ask the community about tips. Like best way to introduce game mechanics in game, or just cool story ideas. Best enemies to use, or any other cool ideas.<br /> <br /> For information purposes my players usually play.<br /> <br /> *Combat heavy, intimidation criminal or dirty cop<br /> *Combat backstabbing face<br /> *Grotesque, like nosferatu<br /> * Academic, doctor or support.<br /> <br /> My plan was to make them create a mortal character and have them start in the hedge, with little memory of what has happened to them. Just the strong urge to run, and a longing for home. And from there introduce game mechanics and the world slowly and in game.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good start. You can establish backstory and background via flashbacks as needed.<br /> <br /> Talk to the players. Find out their interests (both general and Changeling specific - like Dreams, Fetches, Huntsmen, etc.). Also see if they have triggers/off-topic-issues - Changeling is a game about trauma, after all.<br /> <br /> Figure out your area. What are the Hot-spots where major events happen, or the PCs will likely congregate? What are some other area things might happen in? What are each areas' Themes, Mood, and a few face characters? How are they laid out (distances, if that might become a factor, such as racing to area X, or avoiding territory B)? Since it is sandbox, remember to keep things a bit loose, so you can swap elements around if needed (if they never go to the Library for information, move key research NPCs and materials to where they do visit).<br /> <br /> Figure out your big NPCs. Who is allied with whom? Who hates who? Secrets on someone else? Something that might happen if X met Y? Their general attitudes and feelings on big topics. Draw out a web, if you wish to. Include some random characters they know for flavor, if you want.<br /> <br /> Determine the history of the setting. What major events happened recently that resonate through the region? What major events happened in the past that explain the setting, or might come back into relevance? What minor events were important to key characters? What do you see happening that will shape the setting in the future?<br /> <br /> But that's general advice. For Changeling:<br /> <br /> Determine what Courts you want. Seasonal are traditional and have the most built up, but there are other options. The PCs will probably be in them, so they are significant. Figure out the Monarchs, major players, and the <i>feel</i> of them.<br /> <br /> Determine the local mood and stories of the region, because that will impact the Hedge. Trods, local Goblins, Hollows, etc. You don't need specifics, because they can change, but having an idea will help future development.<br /> <br /> Try and work out what the Keepers of the PCs (and major NPCs) are, and any relations between them. They might not show up, but their influence will still be felt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 06-29-2018, 04:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T18:17:33-07:00","id":1232006,"title":"","content":"This mix reminds me of a group that I ran in (locale for game) Kansas City. We called the campaign &quot;A House Divided&quot; and played up the state/ city divide, as well as a court divide. Lots of room for brawling, intrigue, and learning about the past...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5435-mhicwombat","name":"MhicWombat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}